            'faqs' => [
                ['Is Qualifi a university?', '<p>No. Qualifi Ltd is an awarding organisation regulated by Ofqual in England. It designs the qualification, sets the standards and issues the certificate, but it does not run classes. An approved centre teaches you and assesses your work, then claims your certificate from Qualifi. That split is normal for vocational qualifications and it is why the course price comes from the centre, not from Qualifi.</p>', 1],
                ['What is Level 3 equivalent to?', '<p>Level 3 on the Regulated Qualifications Framework is the level reached by A Levels and similar school-leaving qualifications in England. It sits below higher education rather than inside it. That matters for expectations: this is a foundation in business, not a management qualification, and Qualifi positions it as a route towards Level 4 study or the first year of a degree.</p>', 2],
                ['Can I really use this to get onto a degree?', '<p>Qualifi publishes that route, naming the first year of a three-year honours degree at a UK university as a progression option. What it does not do is guarantee you a place. Admission is always the university\'s decision, and different institutions treat Level 3 diplomas differently. If a degree is the goal, speak to the universities you are interested in before you enrol, and ask what they will accept.</p>', 3],
                ['Do I need qualifications to get in?', '<p>Not necessarily. Qualifi lists three ways in: holding a Level 2 qualification, having work experience in a business setting along with clear career goals, or holding a Level 3 qualification in a different subject and wanting to move into business. Entry runs through a centre interview, so the centre makes the judgement on whether you are ready.</p>', 4],
                ['How many optional subjects do I take?', '<p>Qualifi\'s qualification page lists three optional subjects but does not say how many are required, which is a genuine gap in the published information rather than something we are withholding. The Centre Specification document will settle it, and your centre can tell you directly. We would rather point out the gap than guess at a number.</p>', 5],
                ['How long does it take and what does it cost?', '<p>Qualifi publishes neither. There is no total qualification time on the page for this award and no learner price anywhere on the site. Your centre fixes both when it schedules and prices the course, and the answer shifts from one country and one study mode to the next. Treat any advertised duration as the centre\'s figure and ask for the full cost in writing before committing.</p>', 6],
